-- title:
--   Cyclotomic determinant is trivial on inertia away from p
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring and let $\rho$ be an element of [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is: a finite free $A$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_A V = 2$, together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho.\rho$ from the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} \mathbb{Q}$ to $\operatorname{End}_A V$ which is adically continuous in the sense that for every $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} \mathbb{Q}$ such that every automorphism fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho.\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}_A^{\,n} \cdot V$ for all $v \in V$. Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $p \neq q$, and assume `ρ.DetIsCyclotomic p`: the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, and for all $n$, all automorphisms $\sigma$ and all natural numbers $a$, if $\sigma\mu = \mu^{a}$ for every $\mu$ with $\mu^{p^n} = 1$, then $\det(\rho.\rho(\sigma)) - a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$ in $A$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} \mathbb{Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ is a non-unit of $P$, and let $\tau$ be an automorphism lying in `P.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image in the full automorphism group of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then $\det(\rho.\rho(\tau)) = 1$ in $A$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a two-dimensional representation with cyclotomic determinant has determinant $1$ on inertia at any place of residue characteristic $q \neq p$, inertia at such a place acting trivially on $p$-power roots of unity. It is used in the analysis of the local behaviour at $q$ of the representations attached to newforms, in particular when computing characteristic polynomials of inertia and distinguishing principal-series from supercuspidal behaviour.
-- source:
